-- An @nlg on a MIXFIX definition, read at a call site in ANOTHER module.
-- The definitions are in nlg-mixfix-import-lib.l4; the calls are the same, row
-- for row, as nlg-mixfix-local.l4's, so the two outputs can be read side by
-- side. See that file for what each row is.
--
-- One row of that file is left out: a WITH call to `the amount by which`, whose
-- herald trails its last input. Across an IMPORT that call prints the herald
-- as the gloss of `b` as well, for a prefix function just the same, and it is
-- not what this file is about.

IMPORT `nlg-mixfix-import-lib`

#EVAL `the lower of` 840 `and` 160
#EVAL `the amount by which` 840 `exceeds` 160
#EVAL `the shortfall of` 160 `against` 840
#EVAL 840 `plus` 160
#EVAL `the first of` 840 `then` 160
#EVAL `the bare` 840 `and` 160
#EVAL `the greater` 3 4

#EVAL `the lower of` (`the lower of` 5 `and` 6) `and` 7

#EVAL `the lower of` OF 840, 160
#EVAL `the amount by which` OF 840, 160
#EVAL `the lower of` WITH a IS 840, b IS 160
